⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of ARENA
node ARN · ARN · ⟦ARENA:ARN:d5aa0f⟧

WHO   — ARENA — a UD0 book-world — the literary companion to the MTG Arena game-sphere
WHAT  — Arena — the first story Magic ever told: not cosmology but a revenge plot, the ante on the table, and a colorless gunslinger-mage named Garth One-Eye who would become an actual card 27 years later.
WHERE — the city of Estark, where four great Houses of fighter-mages duel in the Arena at Festival, on Dominaria  Framework inputs: the novel (1994, William R. Forstchen, Harper Fantasy — the first MTG novel); early Magic's ante mechanic; the Garth One-Eye card (Modern Horizons 2, 2021)  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0 · Universe David 0)
WHY   — Because before Magic had a Multiverse of lore, it had a Western: a scarred stranger walks into a corrupt city, plays its powers against each other in the dueling circles, and brings the whole rotten order down for revenge.
HOW   — Crystallized from the 1994 novel — a one-eyed wandering mage, Garth, arrives at Festival, turns the four dueling Houses against each other, and avenges a fifth House destroyed a generation before.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  Before Magic had a Multiverse it had Garth — a one-eyed stranger who dueled a corrupt city to ash for revenge, and waited 27 years to become the card he was always made of.

